The layout is guaranteed by `#[repr(C)]`, which makes Rust lay out the struct exactly as C would: `tag` at offset 0, `len` (u32, 4-byte aligned) at offset 4, `flags` (u16, 2-byte aligned) at offset 8, total size 12 bytes (padded from 10 to a multiple of the 4-byte struct alignment). This matches the C struct on every target.

```rust
#[repr(C)]
pub struct PacketHeader {
    pub tag: u8,
    pub len: u32,
    pub flags: u16,
}

#[no_mangle]
pub extern "C" fn packet_header_size() -> usize {
    std::mem::size_of::<PacketHeader>()
}
```
